    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3649" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăristō</span></b> ,
		ōnis, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀρίστων</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a philosopher of Chios</i>, <i>a pupil
				of Zeno</i>, <i>founder of the sceptic
			philosophy</i>, <i>and contemporary of
			Cœsar</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 3, 31, 77</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Leg. 1,
				13</span></i>.— Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aristōnēus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to Aristo</i>, <i>Aristonean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fin. 4, 15, 40</span></i>
			.</div>
